# Round XII Track N2 (2026-07-28) — LIVE REGRESSION FIXTURE (graduated from
# `known_gaps/sound_guard_get_boxed_trait_sigbus.gg`, class 4 of the Round XI
# Track M Guard[Trait] family; net memory-safety close).
#
# CHAINED `m.lock().get().greet()` on `Mutex[Box[Speaker]]`. The compiler
# reads the callee param `Box[Trait]` (16 bytes, `{data, vtable}`) but the
# `Box.new(Robot(…))` argument's slot holds only `Box[Concrete]` (8 bytes,
# `void*`). Pre-fix, the ctor call's memcpy(16) read 8 bytes of stack garbage
# as the vtable pointer → SIGBUS at the first method dispatch through the
# guard. The `sound_` naming convention was the tell (Core #15(d)). Since
# Round XXIV Track B, `gg run` propagates 128+signo as exit 128+N with a
# stderr diagnostic, so a regression here would surface directly.
#
# FIX (Round XII Track N2): the call-arg boundary now packs the concrete Box
# into a `Box[Trait]`-typed temp via `pack_trait_object_for_smart_ptr_ctor`
# (IR helper in `src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs`) — same coercion the LIR
# `try_trait_object_construct` (`src/lir/lower/operands.rs:760`) fires on
# SlotStore. Layering rule 4: one decision site in LIR, IR routes through
# it. Typed-metadata driven (`is_box` + `<Trait>_TraitObj` registration —
# no name-matching per CLAUDE.md "no name matching").
#
# The fix bindings across BOTH C and LLVM lanes (Track N2 RED-verified on
# both). Prints `beep R2` — the D36 intended behavior.
#
# DISTINCT FROM Track J (`sound_guard_get_string_double_free.gg` — double-free
# on non-trait heap-inner via `.get()`'s ownership contract; different root).

from std.collections import Box

trait Speaker:
    String greet(self)

struct Robot:
    String name

equip Robot with Speaker:
    String greet(self):
        return "beep " + self.name

void main():
    print(Mutex[Box[Speaker]](Box.new(Robot("R2"))).lock().get().greet())
